#
# steamlike theme: re-point the Tools gamelist <image> entries at the pre-baked
# 2:3 cover-cards so they render like game capsules in the cover-shelf.
#
# Named "zzz-" so it runs LAST in the common-scripts glob, after 001-sync-modules
# (which `rsync -a --delete`s the pristine svg gamelist into /storage every boot)
# AND after every other first-boot setup script -- so nothing can run after us and
# leave the gamelist pointing back at the .svg icons. The companion essway.service
# drop-in makes ES start only after rocknix-autostart finishes, so this re-point is
# the final word before ES reads the gamelist. Covers ship read-only in
# /usr/share/themecfg/covers (a Theme Manager rebuild writes to
# /storage/.config/themecfg/covers and takes precedence).
#
# --bake-missing first: a tool added by an upstream OTA (e.g. YAPS2, 2026-07)
# has no pre-baked cover yet, so bake one from its icon into the user covers
# dir. The usual case is ZERO missing -> a pure XML scan, no ImageMagick, a few
# ms. Guarded by timeout + followed by a plain --apply so a wedged bake can
# neither block boot nor leave the gamelist un-repointed.

ES_CFG=/storage/.config/emulationstation/es_settings.cfg

# steamlike only -> other themes keep the original square icons
THEME=$(sed -n 's/.*name="ThemeSet" value="\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' "$ES_CFG" 2>/dev/null)
[ "$THEME" = "steamlike" ] || exit 0

timeout 60 python3 /usr/share/themecfg/app/gen_tool_covers.py --bake-missing >/dev/null 2>&1
python3 /usr/share/themecfg/app/gen_tool_covers.py --apply >/dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
